  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "1 Kings",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 22,
    "summary": "Jehoshaphat of Judah and Ahab of Israel join forces against Syria—Ahab’s prophets foretell success—Micaiah foretells the defeat and death of Ahab—Ahab is slain and dogs lick up his blood—Jehoshaphat reigns in righteousness in Judah—Ahaziah reigns in Israel and serves Baal.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And they continued three years without war between Syria and Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:1",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass in the third year, that Jehoshaphat the king of Judah came down to the king of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:2",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king of Israel said unto his servants, Know ye that Ramoth in Gilead is ours, and we be still, and take it not out of the hand of the king of Syria?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 79
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 95
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:3",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said unto Jehoshaphat, Wilt thou go with me to battle to Ramoth-gilead? And Jehoshaphat said to the king of Israel, I am as thou art, my people as thy people, my horses as thy horses.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 123,
            "end": 124,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 3:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 127
          },
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 140
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 3:7.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 3:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 3,
                    "end": 3,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:4",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoshaphat said unto the king of Israel, Inquire, I pray thee, at the word of the Lord to day.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:5",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the king of Israel gathered the prophets together, about four hundred men, and said unto them, Shall I go against Ramoth-gilead to battle, or shall I forbear? And they said, Go up; for the Lord shall deliver it into the hand of the king.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 18:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 213,
            "end": 215
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Kgs. 18:19.",
            "prettyString": "1 Kings 18:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1kings",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 18,
                    "end": 18,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:6",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the Lord besides, that we might inquire of him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:7",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king of Israel said unto Jehoshaphat, There is yet one man, Micaiah the son of Imlah, by whom we may inquire of the Lord: but I hate him; for he doth not prophesy good concerning me, but evil. And Jehoshaphat said, Let not the king say so.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 136,
            "end": 140,
            "text": "TG Hate."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 46,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Hate.",
            "prettyString": "TG Hate",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Hate",
                "entryId": "tg-hate",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:8",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the king of Israel called an officer, and said, Hasten hither Micaiah the son of Imlah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 66
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:9",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king of Israel and Jehoshaphat the king of Judah sat each on his throne, having put on their robes, in a void place in the entrance of the gate of Samaria; and all the prophets prophesied before them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 113,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "HEB threshing floor."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:10",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Zedekiah the son of Chenaanah made him horns of iron: and he said, Thus saith the Lord, With these shalt thou push the Syrians, until thou have consumed them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:11",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And all the prophets prophesied so, saying, Go up to Ramoth-gilead, and prosper: for the Lord shall deliver it into the king’s hand.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 110
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:12",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And the messenger that was gone to call Micaiah spake unto him, saying, Behold now, the words of the prophets declare good unto the king with one mouth: let thy word, I pray thee, be like the word of one of them, and speak that which is good.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 117
          },
          {
            "start": 223,
            "end": 236
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:13",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And Micaiah said, As the Lord liveth, what the Lord saith unto me, that will I speak.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:14",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "So he came to the king. And the king said unto him, Micaiah, shall we go against Ramoth-gilead to battle, or shall we forbear? And he answered him, Go, and prosper: for the Lord shall deliver it into the hand of the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 192,
            "end": 194
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:15",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king said unto him, How many times shall I adjure thee that thou tell me nothing but that which is true in the name of the Lord?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "1 Kings 22:16",
        "book": "1 Kings",
        "chapter": 22,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said, I saw all Israel scattered upon the hills, as sheep that have not a shepherd: and the Lord said, These have no master: let them return every man to his house in peace.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 39,
            "text": "TG Israel, Scattering of."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Sheep; Shepherd."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
